VariateFlags:   1 - variate independently
   2 - variate transformed value 
   3 - calculate one g-tensor value based on constant average and 2 other values.
   4 - tensor value is equal to y-value
   5 - tensor value is equal to x-value 
   6 - g2(A2) tensor values are equal to g1(A1)
   7 - angles of A-tensor (or linewidth tensor) are inverse to those of g1-tensor (this means, this tensor is in the molecular frame)
   7 - angles of Diffusion tensor are equal to those of g1-tensor (this means, diffusion tensor is in g1 frame)
   8 - angles of A-tensor (or linewidth tensor) are equal to those of g2-tensor

Possible Algorithm keywords: COBYLA, BOBYQA, PRAXIS, NELDERMEAD, SBPLX, details see http://ab-initio.mit.edu/wiki/index.php/NLopt_Algorithms 

Euler angles of all magnetic tensors, except g1 and Diffusion, convert magnetic tensors into g1 tensor.
DiffusionEuler angles convert Diffusion frame into molecular orientation frame.
g1Euler angles convert g1 frame into molecular orientation frame. D-tensor is coaxial with g1 tensor
#IntegrateGauss and IntegrateGaussKronrod flags indicate wheter it is necessary to integrate spectra over ODF on two progressive nets (IntegrateGaussKronrod) or not (IntegrateGauss)

To safely stop the calculation on the current iteration, create the file named "stop" in the working directory
